 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051081 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "7fa30ad3-9041-5912-9f1e-90bd24bebbe8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124585 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049477 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124585 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049699 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124585 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186051081 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124585 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186125238 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124585 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186125239 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124585 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186284746 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124585 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186357748 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124585 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186360456 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124585 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186360457 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124585 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186360458 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124585 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186360474 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124585 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186398624 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124585 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186399275 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124585 #edb/ref 1039 "Identifying Properties of Elliptic Cones" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124585 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186124396 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124585 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "2e0b4012-403b-5739-8f33-3c79111129fd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124586 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186124893 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124586 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186124894 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124586 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186284747 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124586 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186321020 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124586 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186357749 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124586 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186357750 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124586 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186357751 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124586 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186360601 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124586 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186381890 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124586 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186381903 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124586 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186382601 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124586 #edb/ref 1039 "Finding Traces of Elliptic Cones" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124586 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186124397 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124586 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "fb7148a2-58cc-5023-845c-435b47e31c83" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124697 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186125513 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124697 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186125514 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124697 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186125515 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124697 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186125516 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124697 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186125640 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124697 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124697 #edb/ref 1045 "Elliptic Cones" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124697 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186125513 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124697 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186050456 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124697 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "665ce843-c897-5cef-9141-25ecb7cdc260" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125513 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186125514 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125513 #edb/ref 1061 30715 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125513 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "8afa0f97-79d7-5556-8054-cf7a927fbc25" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125513 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186125828 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125514 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186125640 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125514 #edb/ref 1061 30716 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125514 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "b83d2704-1cd8-5d3e-a5d6-3347b6842a7c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125514 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186124585 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125515 #edb/ref 1061 30717 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125515 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "60b53775-0c8d-50d6-8793-5131aef5e1ab" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125515 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186124586 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125516 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186125515 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125516 #edb/ref 1061 30720 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125516 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "63150029-88d0-527b-9d21-8af46b91197c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125516 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186125829 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125640 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186125516 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125640 #edb/ref 1061 45285 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125640 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "b8cf188e-213a-5603-a9b9-fc97304c8d5c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125640 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186125882 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125828 #edb/ref 1064 "Consider the quadric surface\n\n$$z^2 = x^2 + y^2$$\n\nwhose graph is shown below.\n\n![](images/d5/d5a23dfa8bf6a0efec59763b9a2ec6d22d878f75babdbed9fc04dc8a7106f6ba.png)\n\nThis is an example of an **elliptic cone**. It has its **vertex** at the origin, and the $z$-axis is the **axis of symmetry** of the cone.\n\nMore generally, the equation of an elliptic cone whose vertex is at $(x_0, y_0, z_0)$ is given by\n\n$$(z-z_0)^2 = \\dfrac{(x-x_0)^2}{a^2} + \\dfrac{(y-y_0)^2}{b^2},$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125828 #edb/ref 1065 4924 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125828 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "bf9fab37-b71c-5d84-95d5-791cd41706a7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125828 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125829 #edb/ref 1064 "So far, we've encountered cones whose axes of symmetry are parallel to the $z$-axis. \nLet's now consider the cases when a cone is oriented along the $x$- or the $y$-axes.\n\nFor an elliptic cone centered at the origin, the other two cases are as follows:\n\n- When the $y^2$ term is isolated on one side, the axis of symmetry is the $y$-axis.\n\n$$\ny^2 = \\dfrac{x^2}{a^2} + \\dfrac{z^2}{c^2}\n$$\n\n![](images/06/06c02be2e3ee96862abacc19885e34a8b3cb096a1b85417169022394839e7888.png)\n\n- When the $x^2$ term is isolated on one side, the axis of symmetry is the $x$-axis.\n\n$$\nx^2 = \\dfrac{y^2}{b^2} + \\dfrac{z^2}{c^2}\n$$\n\n![](images/0e/0ef83c7e023ddcf5e408c7b8cb4e97deb7ece2f366628e019aa04ef90810c6f9.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125829 #edb/ref 1065 4925 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125829 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "3ba615cd-207c-53f0-ac45-57c3b3f46b84" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125829 #edb/ref 1067 "Alternative Orientations of the Axis of Symmetry" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125882 #edb/ref 1064 "The traces of an elliptic cone are either intersecting lines, ellipses, hyperbolas, or points.\n\nFor example, let's find the traces with the coordinate planes for the elliptic cone given by\n\n$$\nz^2 = x^2 + y^2\n$$\n\n- The trace of this surface in the $xy$-plane (when $z=0$) is given by the equation\n\n$$\nx^2 + y^2 = 0,\n$$\n\nwhich corresponds to the origin $(0,0,0).$\n\n![](images/d5/d5a23dfa8bf6a0efec59763b9a2ec6d22d878f75babdbed9fc04dc8a7106f6ba.png)\n\n- The trace of this surface in the $xz$-plane (when $y=0$) is given by the equation\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{0}^{2} & ={z}^{2} \\\\ {x}^{2} & ={z}^{2} \\\\ x & =\\pm z,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich corresponds to two lines in the $xz$-plane.\n\n![](images/ba/ba552154b10ae7919496031613005c60461272923c6cae262a757b6df89c398d.png)\n\n- The trace of this surface in the $yz$-plane (when $x=0$) is given by the equation\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{0}^{2}+{y}^{2} & ={z}^{2} \\\\ {y}^{2} & ={z}^{2} \\\\ y & =\\pm z,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich corresponds to two lines in the $yz$-plane.\n\n![](images/2e/2e22ee99e93475eabae9ce8caacee814d0066dd30042367668542485cdacd8a3.png)\n\nThere are a few other cases we should note:\n\n- The trace of our surface with the plane $z=k$ for $k \\neq 0$ is an ellipse:\n\n$$\nx^2+y^2 = k^2\n$$\n\n![](images/d3/d32e0c05b0bd5a55ff38183b362eebd44bf668dc9ee68ec5b6ae2274fdae934e.png)\n\n- The traces of our surface with the plane $x=k$ or $y=k$ for $k \\neq 0$ are hyperbolas:\n\n$$\nz^2-y^2 = k^2 \\qquad \\textrm{or}\\qquad z^2-x^2 = k^2\n$$\n\n![](images/23/23dd8112391406afd1da714df32d3a01ddb99b68c3b0885078ad76ebba23f9b5.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125882 #edb/ref 1065 7841 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125882 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "efd10d7e-d93a-5f24-b896-67f70dc4aa16" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125882 #edb/ref 1067 "Traces of Elliptic Cones" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186354752 #edb/ref 1080 "z=-\\frac{y}{3}\\pm 1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186354752 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186354752 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "096807f4-6104-5c9d-9a4f-3cc078997926" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186355284 #edb/ref 1080 "z=\\pm \\frac{y}{9}+1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186355284 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186355284 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "45b089cf-4cd4-5955-98fe-9f0ff803df9a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186355315 #edb/ref 1080 "(2,0,0)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186355315 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186355315 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "497c9287-8527-5f28-9070-29d5455ff937" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186355718 #edb/ref 1080 "z=\\pm \\frac{y}{3}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186355718 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186355718 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "78a27687-7772-5319-a40c-aef31e7c2570" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186355784 #edb/ref 1080 "z=-\\frac{y}{3}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186355784 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186355784 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "7fd6a87d-0609-5bbe-9ab6-30cf1a7bcfa3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186355877 #edb/ref 1080 "y=\\pm 3x-5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186355877 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186355877 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "8935fc20-662f-5493-8895-2ff5e7873ee9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186355907 #edb/ref 1080 "y=\\pm \\frac{x}{3}+2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186355907 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186355907 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "8cd8d2b3-1b54-51b9-aa4b-86e2141de38d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186356000 #edb/ref 1080 "(9,2,0)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186356000 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186356000 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "97966c4c-9e1f-5c8e-b01d-facfe4e419d2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186356003 #edb/ref 1080 "z=\\pm \\frac{y}{9}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186356003 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186356003 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "97dcd38b-595a-5837-97a8-ed1062f9f32b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186356269 #edb/ref 1080 "y=\\pm \\frac{2x}{3}+18" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186356269 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186356269 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "b6f64f22-7913-52f4-86c8-f51e90ac0c11" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186356907 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186354752 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186356907 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186355284 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186356907 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186355718 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186356907 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186355784 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186356907 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186356003 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186356907 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186356907 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186356907 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186355718 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186356907 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "0000aeb3-77f2-52e8-8fd1-917fe7c0e597" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357148 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186355315 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357148 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186355877 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357148 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186355907 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357148 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186356000 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357148 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186356269 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357148 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357148 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357148 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186355315 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357148 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "8196235b-25ca-50fc-919f-d7ee8e52fb0e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357749 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186356907 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357749 #edb/ref 1069 "q-94486" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357749 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357749 #edb/ref 1071 "What is the trace in the $yz$-plane of the elliptic cone $\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}={z}^{2}\\,?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357749 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "1057b215-35c6-5a51-b1d3-2145bec593cc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357749 #edb/ref 1074 "To find the trace in the $yz$-plane, we substitute $x=0$ into the equation of the elliptic cone, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{0}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9} & ={z}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{9} & ={z}^{2} \\\\ z & =\\pm \\frac{y}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us two lines in the $yz$-plane with equations $z=\\pm \\frac{y}{3}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357751 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186357148 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357751 #edb/ref 1069 "q-94496" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357751 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357751 #edb/ref 1071 "What is the trace in the $xy$-plane of the elliptic cone $9(x-2)^{2}+2{y}^{2}=18{z}^{2}\\,?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357751 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d2cfd332-5d5c-5209-92ee-4f9962118084" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357751 #edb/ref 1074 "To find the trace in the $xy$-plane, we substitute $z=0$ into the equation of the elliptic cone, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9(x-2)^{2}+2{y}^{2}=18(0)^{2} \\\\ 9(x-2)^{2}+2{y}^{2}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives in the $xy$-plane the point $(2,0,0).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
